# pdf-to-pdfa — both paths, one real validator, one outside reader (current build)
# Driver: docs/research/engine-state-rail.mjs, one fresh Chromium per state (BLOCK=1 cuts cdn.jsdelivr.net both in
#   Chrome's resolver and through CDP, so the fallback is the network's, not the tab's). 9 runs, parts 1b/2b/3b.
# Verdicts: `sh docs/research/pdfa-validator.sh <part> <file>` — veraPDF 1.28.2 (greenfield CLI, the only PDF/A
#   validator that exists; it cannot run in a tab, so the card's own “no validator ran” stays true).
# Structures: `docs/research/pdfa-switch-readers.py` reads the same bytes back with PyMuPDF, pypdf-shaped lookups,
#   an ICC header walk and lcms2, and every claim is checked against the *claimed* part.
#
